1. FRAMEWORK & DUAL-MODEL ADOPTION ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================
WorkSphere is engineered and licensed by Praveen Chavan under two distinct commercial 
engagement models designed to serve operating employers and technology providers:

  (A) MODEL 1: Hosted Subscription (SaaS) — For employers, HR teams, and corporate 
      organisations seeking a fully managed, turn-key cloud platform with zero DevOps overhead.

  (B) MODEL 2: Licence with Source Code — For IT companies, managed service providers (MSPs), 
      software houses, and system integrators seeking to own the codebase, self-host, 
      rebrand/white-label, customize, and deliver solutions to their own client base.

All rights not expressly granted in this Licence or in an executed bilateral written 
agreement signed by Praveen Chavan are strictly reserved.

================================================================================
2. MODEL 1: HOSTED SUBSCRIPTION (SOFTWARE AS A SERVICE — SaaS)
================================================================================
For organisations adopting WorkSphere as a cloud service:

2.1. Grant of Use:
Subject to prompt payment of the applicable subscription fees, Praveen Chavan grants 
the subscribing organisation a non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable right to access 
and operate the hosted WorkSphere cloud platform through authorized user accounts 
solely for its internal human resources, payroll, and workforce operations.

2.2. Isolated Tenant Workspace:
Each subscribing organisation is provisioned an isolated workspace and dedicated tenant 
database boundary, ensuring multi-company data privacy, role-based access control (RBAC), 
and compliance with statutory confidentiality requirements.

2.3. Managed Infrastructure & Updates:
TalentHub hosts, monitors, backups, and maintains the hosted infrastructure. Subscriptions 
include routine platform upgrades, statutory payroll and tax formula updates, bug fixes, 
and performance optimizations deployed automatically with zero server maintenance on the client.

2.4. Subscription Tiers & Billing Cycles:
Fees are determined by the customer's selected plan tier, employee headcount, and billing 
frequency (monthly, quarterly, or yearly) as specified on the commercial invoice.

2.5. Demo & Live Evaluation:
Customers may commence use through a complimentary 7-day sandbox demo followed by a guided 
live evaluation period. Transition to a paid plan occurs upon mutual agreement.

2.6. Source Code Exclusion:
UNDER MODEL 1, NO SOURCE CODE, DATABASE REPOSITORIES, OR DEVELOPER ASSETS ARE DELIVERED, 
LICENSED, OR TRANSFERRED. THE CLIENT RECEIVES ONLY THE BENEFIT OF THE MANAGED CLOUD SERVICE.

================================================================================
3. MODEL 2: COMMERCIAL LICENCE WITH SOURCE CODE (FOR IT & SOFTWARE COMPANIES)
================================================================================
For IT companies, software consultancies, and system integrators wishing to own and adapt the product:

3.1. Individual Scoping & Written Legal Agreement:
A company seeking to license WorkSphere together with its underlying source code must enter 
into a binding, written commercial agreement with Praveen Chavan / TalentHub prior to delivery. 
No source code handover occurs without an executed written agreement and agreed payment milestone schedule.

3.2. Scope of Delivery:
Upon execution of the bilateral written agreement, Praveen Chavan shall hand over:
  (a) The complete application codebase (PHP 8.2 / CodeIgniter 4 framework layer);
  (b) Complete MariaDB/MySQL database schemas, migrations, seeds, and index definitions;
  (c) Front-end assets, CSS design tokens, and client JavaScript components;
  (d) Technical architecture blueprints, developer documentation, and deployment guides.

3.3. Self-Hosting & Operational Freedom:
The licensee possesses the right to deploy and host the platform on its own cloud infrastructure 
(including AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, or private data centers) or on client-dedicated servers.

3.4. White-Labelling & Rebranding:
Subject to the written agreement terms, the licensee is granted the right to rebrand, re-skin, 
modify user interfaces, bind custom domain names, apply custom corporate logos, and customize client 
portals to present the software under the licensee's own commercial brand.

3.5. Extension & Client Redistribution:
The licensee may engineer custom proprietary modules, integrate third-party APIs, and offer 
the configured solution or services to its own commercial clientele within the contractual boundaries 
stipulated in the written agreement.

================================================================================
4. CORE CONTRACTUAL & DISCUSSION PILLARS FOR SOURCE CODE LICENCES
================================================================================
A licence discussion between Praveen Chavan / TalentHub and an IT company normally covers 
seven foundational commercial and technical pillars:

  1. Rights & Limits: The specific rights granted to the licensee (deployment boundaries, 
     hosting scope, client volume, and geographical or vertical limits) defined in writing.
  
  2. Source Code & Documentation: Scope of the repository, database schemas, integration 
     guides, and architectural documentation handed over to the licensee's technical team.
  
  3. Deployment & Knowledge-Transfer Support: Hands-on setup assistance, server hardening, 
     CI/CD pipeline onboarding, and technical knowledge transfer from TalentHub engineers.
  
  4. Branding & White-Labelling: Permitted scope of cosmetic, domain, and portal re-branding 
     to ensure seamless alignment with the licensee's corporate brand.
  
  5. Customisation Built to Order: Specifications, timelines, and deliverables for bespoke 
     features, custom shift rules, or specialized enterprise integrations developed by TalentHub.
  
  6. Support & Maintenance Period: Defined post-handover warranty, framework security patches, 
     bug fixes, and SLA-backed engineering consultation period.
  
  7. Price & Payment Milestones: Structured, transparent commercial terms and payment milestones 
     aligned with delivery phases, technical verification, and formal sign-offs.

These are discussion points, not a fixed price list. We scope each licence individually and put 
the outcome in a written agreement. Organisations that only want to use WorkSphere do not need 
a licence: a subscription gives full use of the hosted service.

